   "text": "I read the structure as a macrocyclic peptide with a thioether bridge, and I wrote it as SMILES starting from the C-terminal lysine.\n\n**Sequence, N-terminus to C-terminus:** thioacetyl\u2013Phe\u2013Val\u2013Pro\u2013Thr\u2013Thr\u2013Bip\u2013N-Me-Ala\u2013Bip\u2013N-Me-Ala\u2013Glu\u2013Ala\u2013Pro\u2013Cys\u2013Gly\u2013Lys-NH2. Bip is 4-biphenylalanine. The thioacetyl CH2 is joined by a thioether (S) to the Cys side-chain CH2, which closes the macrocycle. The lysine \u03b5-NH carries the wavy bond, which I wrote as `*`.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I assigned each stereocentre from its wedge or hash and compared it with the L-amino-acid pattern.\n- Lys, Cys, Phe, Val, both Thr (including the \u03b2-carbons), both Bip, both N-Me-Ala, Glu, Ala and the left-hand Pro all come out as the natural L configuration.\n- The Pro next to Val has a solid wedge on its ring CH2 and comes out as D-Pro (R), which is a less common residue. I kept it as drawn.\n\nI checked the SMILES for valid ring closures and for atom-by-atom agreement with the drawing.\n\nSMILES: *NCCCC[C@@H](C(N)=O)NC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@@H]1CSCC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccccc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N2CCC[C@@H]2C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc3ccc(cc3)-c3ccccc3)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc3ccc(cc3)-c3ccccc3)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](C)C(=O)N3CCC[C@H]3C(=O)N1"
